usage: run_test.py [-h] [-t TEST [TEST ...]] [--testlist TESTLIST]
                   [-g GROUP [GROUP ...]] [-f FILTER [FILTER ...]]
                   [--list [{tests,groups}]] [-r RUNDIR] [-o] [-k] [-b] [-p]
                   [-s] [-j JOBS] [-c TIMEOUT_CLOCKS] [-v LOG_LEVEL]
                   [--coverage] [--coverage_only] [--dry_run] [--log_wave]
                   [--log_vcd] [--log_kanata]

Run RTL simulation.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -t TEST [TEST ...], --test TEST [TEST ...]
                        Specify one or more tests to run (space-separated)
  --testlist TESTLIST   Path to a YAML file containing a list of tests.
                        Defaults to '<repo_root>/testlist.yaml'
                        unless -t|--test is used
  -g GROUP [GROUP ...], --group GROUP [GROUP ...]
                        Select test groups (top level keys) from the testlist.
                        Tokens regex-match group names and exact-match bundle
                        aliases from _bundles. Pass as space-separated values.
                        Use ~ to exclude. E.g., '-g riscv_isa "~rv32m"'
                        includes all groups matching 'riscv_isa', except those
                        matching 'rv32m'. Quote tokens with shell-special
                        chars (e.g. '~', '[', '*') to avoid shell expansion.
                        If not specified, all groups are selected
  -f FILTER [FILTER ...], --filter FILTER [FILTER ...]
                        Select individual tests from the selected groups.
                        Tokens regex-match the repo-relative test path with
                        the extension stripped (e.g.
                        'sim/sw/baremetal/ukr_m_dotv/int16_al'), so a token
                        can name a directory, a file, or any substring of
                        either. Use ~ to exclude. E.g., '-f ukr_m_dotv
                        "~ual"'. Same quoting rules as --group arg above.
                        Applied after -g|--group. Use --list to see the
                        available test names. If not specified, all tests in
                        the selected group(s) are run
  --list [{tests,groups}]
                        List the testlist contents and exit, without building
                        or simulating. 'tests' (default) prints each group
                        with its expanded test names, exactly as -f|--filter
                        matches them; 'groups' prints one line per group.
                        Honors -g|--group and -f|--filter
  -r RUNDIR, --rundir RUNDIR
                        Optional custom run directory name
  -o, --build_only      Only build the testbench
  -k, --keep_build      Reuse existing build if available
  -b, --rebuild_all     Rebuild everything: RTL, ISA sim, cosim. Takes
                        priority over -k if both are specified
  -p, --keep_pass       Keep rundir of passed tests. Applicable only if -k is
                        used
  -s, --stop_on_fail    Stop execution after the first test failure
  -j JOBS, --jobs JOBS  Number of parallel jobs to run (default: number of CPU
                        cores)
  -c TIMEOUT_CLOCKS, --timeout_clocks TIMEOUT_CLOCKS
                        Number of clocks before simulations times out
  -v LOG_LEVEL, --log_level LOG_LEVEL
                        Log level during simulation
  --coverage            Build instrumented for code coverage, then merge per-
                        test DBs and generate an HTML report after the suite
  --coverage_only       Only merge coverage and generate the report. Relies on
                        existing instrumented test directories from a prior
                        --coverage run
  --dry_run             Print tests that would run without building or
                        simulating
  --log_wave            Collect .wdb waveform, all modules from the top down
  --log_vcd             Collect .vcd waveform, all modules from the top down
  --log_kanata          Collect kanata log
